## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to extend Dijkstra's algorithm to count shortest paths while handling ties and modular arithmetic—a common pattern in competitive programming and graph algorithms.

## Key Concepts
- Dijkstra's algorithm with path counting augmentation
- Non-negative edge weights, including zero-weight edges
- Modular arithmetic for large path counts and overflow prevention
- Edge case handling: unreachable destinations, multiple optimal paths, zero-weight cycles

## Code Example
```javascript
function countShortestPaths(n, edges, s, t) {
  const MOD = 1e9 + 7;
  const dist = new Array(n).fill(Infinity);
  const ways = new Array(n).fill(0);

  dist[s] = 0;
  ways[s] = 1;

  const pq = new MinPriorityQueue({ priority: x => dist[x] });
  pq.enqueue(s);

  while (!pq.isEmpty()) {
    const u = pq.dequeue().element;

    for (const [v, w] of edges[u]) {
      if (dist[u] + w < dist[v]) {
        dist[v] = dist[u] + w;
        ways[v] = ways[u];
        pq.enqueue(v);
      } else if (dist[u] + w === dist[v]) {
        ways[v] = (ways[v] + ways[u]) % MOD;
      }
    }
  }

  return { distance: dist[t] === Infinity ? -1 : dist[t], paths: ways[t] };
}
```

## Time & Space Complexity
- **Time**: O((N + M) log N) due to priority queue operations
- **Space**: O(N) for distance and path count arrays

## Why This Question Is Asked
This question tests dynamic programming intuition on a constrained path counting problem with simple transitions and boundary conditions.

## Key Concepts
- **Recurrence relation:** f(i) = f(i+1) + f(i+2) with modulo arithmetic
- **Memoization vs. tabulation:** Trade-offs between recursive top-down with caching versus iterative bottom-up approaches
- **Edge conditions:** Blocked start/end positions, single-cell arrays

## Code Example
```javascript
function countPaths(blocked) {
  const n = blocked.length;
  const MOD = 1000000007;
  if (blocked[0]) return 0;

  // Memoized DFS
  const memo = Array(n).fill(-1);
  function dfs(i) {
    if (i === n - 1) return blocked[i] ? 0 : 1;
    if (i >= n || blocked[i]) return 0;
    if (memo[i] !== -1) return memo[i];
    memo[i] = (dfs(i + 1) + dfs(i + 2)) % MOD;
    return memo[i];
  }
  return dfs(0);
}

// Bottom-up DP (O(1) space)
function countPathsDP(blocked) {
  const n = blocked.length;
  const MOD = 1000000007;
  if (blocked[0]) return 0;

  let next2 = 1, next1 = blocked[n - 1] ? 0 : 1;
  for (let i = n - 2; i >= 0; i--) {
    const curr = blocked[i] ? 0 : (next1 + next2) % MOD;
    next2 = next1;
    next1 = curr;
  }
  return next1;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to fuse graph shortest-path ideas with node activation delays and cycle handling, plus choosing between DAG DP and general graph Dijkstra.

## Key Concepts
- Dijkstra with transformed edge costs w(u,v)+d(v)
- Topological sort for DAG optimization
- Handling multiple sources S
- Non-negative weights guarantee correctness

## Code Example
```javascript
function earliestFinish(V, adj, S, d) {
  const INF = Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY;
  const dist = new Array(V).fill(INF);
  const pq = new MinHeap((a,b)=>a[0]-b[0]);
  for (const s of S) { dist[s] = d[s]; pq.push([dist[s], s]); }
  while (!pq.isEmpty()) {
    const [du, u] = pq.pop();
    if (du !== dist[u]) continue;
    for (const [v, w] of adj[u]) {
      const cand = dist[u] + w + d[v];
      if (cand < dist[v]) { dist[v] = cand; pq.push([cand, v]); }
    }
  }
  return dist;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to combine topo sort with DP and counting paths; ensures handling of unreachable nodes and modulo arithmetic.

## Key Concepts
- Topological sorting
- DP on DAG
- Shortest path counting modulo
- Edge relaxation and correctness sketch

## Code Example
```javascript
function shortestPathsInDAG(n, edges) {
  const adj = Array.from({length:n}, ()=>[]);
  const indeg = Array(n).fill(0);
  for (const [u,v,w] of edges) { adj[u].push([v,w]); indeg[v]++; }
  const topo = [];
  const q = [];
  for (let i=0;i<n;i++) if (indeg[i]===0) q.push(i);
  for (let i=0;i<q.length;i++) {
    const u = q[i]; topo.push(u);
    for (const [v] of adj[u]) if (--indeg[v]===0) q.push(v);
  }
  const INF = Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY;
  const dist = Array(n).fill(INF);
  const ways = Array(n).fill(0);
  const MOD = 1_000_000_007;
  dist[0] = 0; ways[0] = 1;
  for (const u of topo) {
    if (dist[u]===INF) continue;
    for (const [v,w] of adj[u]) {
      const nd = dist[u] + w;
      if (nd < dist[v]) { dist[v] = nd; ways[v] = ways[u]; }
      else if (nd === dist[v]) { ways[v] = (ways[v] + ways[u]) % MOD; }
    }
  }
  return {dist, ways};
}
```

